  "schema": "hm-soundmap/1",
  "$doc": "The score's sound map (WP-04, audio/score.mjs). reference: the key every tonal note is written in (v2's C5 major pentatonic, audio/soundtrack.mjs N); notes are transposed to the Mallow's kit by scale degree (audio/pitch.mjs). kits: the app's Mallow kits (hushmallow/src/engine/audio.js KITS: root Hz, scale semitones, gesture speed), copied here so Node can plan without the page; the render page re-checks every value against the engine and fails on any difference (audio/render-offline.mjs), and tests/unit/audio-pitch.test.mjs checks them against the app source. mallows: kit and home bed per Mallow (registry realm), plus the Mallow's own sound pack. realms: the engine bed (REALM_BEDS id) and the layers each time of day adds; 'default' is the explicit entry for any time of day not listed. cues: the legacy cue type -> recipe map, used only for cue logs that carry no move ownership (the frozen v2 route); a composed direction names each cue's recipe in its move (composer/moves, cues: {type: {recipe}}). kits[].voice: the tonal content of the kit's own voice, transcribed from the engine (src names the lines): note = the components of one kit note relative to its pitch (f0 at the onset, f1 where its glide lands, glide seconds, relative level, vib = vibrato depth in cents when there is one; static partials omitted); success.events = the closing phrase the logo plays (MO-CLOSE): dt seconds (times the kit speed unless unscaled, plus 'plus' unscaled seconds), deg = the kit scale degree of its base pitch, part note|accent, comps relative to the base (base = clamp(D(deg) x mult) when given). audio/score.mjs models the phrase for the closing-contour rule; tests/parity/audio-score.test.mjs traces the engine's oscillators and holds this table to them.",
